    \citet{impagliazzo2001problems} showed that under ETH, no 3-SAT algorithm runs in $2^{o(M)}$ time on all instances with $M$ clauses. We consider a variant of 3-SAT, called 3-SAT-2-ltr, where every literal appears at most twice.
