codex
Implemented and verified the tournament-fixing problem generator based on the paper’s ETH-tight `ell = log₂(n)` regime ([arXiv:2601.08530](https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.08530)).

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2601.08530/gen_2601_08530.py)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2601.08530/README.md)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2601.08530/selftest_report.json)
- [Hardening transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2601.08530/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Harness metadata](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2601.08530/.meta.json)

Results:

- All G1–G8 gates pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four adversary attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Canonical-key tests: 60/60 relabelings and 20/20 distinct instances.
- Four-vendor harness verdict: `hardened` at 256 players without escalation.
- Two earlier statistically planted constructions were rejected after greedy and construction-aware attacks solved them; this history is documented.

The README explicitly notes the main limitation: the exact subset algorithm was resource-capped, and a bespoke SAT-gadget decoder remains untested.
